      "element_id": "prisma_2020_1_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_16",
      "quote": "CHWled blood pressure and Diabetes control interventions for NCD prevention and control in developing countries: a systematic review of randomised controlled trials Patient or population: patients with NCD prevention and control in developing countries: a systematic review of randomised controlled trials",
      "reason": "The title/heading text specifies the intervention (CHW-led blood pressure and diabetes control interventions / CHW delivered primary prevention interventions) and the population/setting (NCD prevention and control in developing countries), providing key information about the main objective/population and intervention."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_1_e3",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The title does not provide supplementary information such as the analysis method, included study designs, update status, or living-review status. No evidence in the title indicates study designs or analysis details."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 85
}

{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_3",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_8",
      "quote": "However, studies assessing their effectiveness in delivering primary prevention interventions for non-communicable disease prevention and control in LMIC settings are limited,[10], though this has been proven for developed countries.[11]",
      "reason": "The manuscript describes the current state of knowledge and uncertainty by stating that studies assessing CHW effectiveness for NCD prevention in LMICs are limited, contrasting this with evidence from developed countries."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_8",
      "quote": "Considering this deficiency in availability of effectiveness parameters, a systematic review on effectiveness of CHW delivered primary prevention interventions for NCDs in developing countries was conducted by the authors.",
      "reason": "The authors explicitly state the importance and need for conducting the review because of the deficiency of effectiveness data in LMIC settings and therefore conducted the systematic review."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e3",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_8",
      "quote": "Only four systematic reviews assessing this effectiveness in LMIC/ developing countries could be identified after review of published literature.[11-14]",
      "reason": "The manuscript identifies existing systematic reviews (four) and thereby situates the current review in relation to prior reviews, explaining the landscape of prior evidence."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e4",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_3",
      "quote": "A community health worker (CHW) delivers NCD preventive services using informational as well as behavioural approaches. Community education and interpersonal communication on lifestyle modifications is imparted with focus on primordial prevention of NCDs and screening is conducted as part of early diagnosis and management.",
      "reason": "The manuscript briefly describes how the intervention (CHW-delivered services) is intended to work—through informational and behavioural approaches, education, lifestyle modification counseling, and screening—constituting a proposed mechanism of action."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e5",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "No evidence was found in the provided text that a logic model was presented or considered to show hypothesised relationships between intervention components and outcomes."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 85
}

{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_4",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_4_e1",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_8",
      "quote": "Considering this deficiency in availability of effectiveness parameters, a systematic review on effectiveness of CHW delivered primary prevention interventions for NCDs in developing countries was conducted by the authors. This was conducted following the hypothesis that for NCD control programs employing a community health worker is more likely to be successful than routine care. This manuscript details the methodologies followed and reports on findings from this systematic review.",
      "reason": "The authors state that they conducted a systematic review on the effectiveness of CHW-delivered primary prevention interventions for NCDs and state a hypothesis comparing CHW programs to routine care, which indicates the review objective. However, there is no explicit, structured statement of specific review question(s) using a question-formulation framework (e.g., PICO or explicit primary/secondary objectives), so the requirement is only partially met."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_4_e2",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_12",
      "quote": "Interventions included community health worker led health education/health promotion (life style modification advice) for diabetes, cancer, cardiovascular diseases and stroke prevention. Health topics that were studied include healthy diet, physical activity/ regular exercise, tobacco consumption/ promotion of smoking cessation, alcohol consumption, management of type 2 diabetes/ hypertension, awareness for common cancers. Studies were excluded if the intervention was not adequately described to determine that it was a CHW intervention or if the effects were not properly described to determine whether the CHWs presence produced the effects.",
      "reason": "The review specifies the population and interventions of interest (CHW-led health education/promotion for various NCDs and risk factors) and exclusion criteria, and Table 1 provides examples of populations, interventions and controls. However, the authors do not present an explicit PICO-formatted planned comparison statement (e.g., 'Population X compared to Y with intervention Z vs comparator A') nor a clear, complete PICO table; thus planned comparisons are described in the text but not explicitly framed using PICO, making this only partially satisfied."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 65
}

{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_5",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_13",
      "quote": "Only randomised controlled trials (community based randomised controlled trial, cluster randomised trials) published in the last 15 years (2000-2015) were included in the review. ... Trials about CHWs working in NCD related promotional, preventive or curative primary healthcare in LMICs/ developing countries were included. ... A seven point inclusion criterion was followed to shortlist the articles. A research was considered eligible for inclusion if it followed a randomised controlled study design in community settings of low middle income countries with community health worker as intervention delivery person for general or high risk population for primary prevention of NCDs as compared to routine care or enhanced routine care as comparator.",
      "reason": "The manuscript specifies key study characteristics used for eligibility: study designs (randomised controlled trials, cluster RCTs), settings (community settings in LMICs/developing countries), intervention delivery (CHW), target populations (general or high-risk for primary prevention of NCDs), and the time window (2000-2015)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_13",
      "quote": "Only randomised controlled trials (community based randomised controlled trial, cluster randomised trials) published in the last 15 years (2000-2015) were included in the review. ... Searches of published literature ... were done ... without restriction to language: PubMed (2000-2015); Excerpta Medica Database (EMBASE) (2000-2015); OVID (2000-2015) and World PLOS Health Organization (WHO) library and Cochrane library. Clinical trials registers such as ClinicalTrials.gov ... were another source of information that were reviewed for relevant literature. ... Unpublished reports identified in a database or referenced in a publication in the initial search were also read.",
      "reason": "The review states eligibility restrictions by dissemination year (2000-2015), explicitly states no language restriction, and that unpublished reports and trial registers were considered, addressing publication/report status criteria."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e3",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_16",
      "quote": "We recorded all missing secondary outcome data in the data extraction form and in the risk of bias table. One trial lacking baseline information collection by investigators was excluded from the meta-analysis.",
      "reason": "The review documents that missing outcome data were recorded and that a trial lacking baseline information was excluded from meta-analysis, but it does not explicitly distinguish exclusions due to outcomes not being measured versus outcomes measured but not reported."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e4",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_16",
      "quote": "Meta-analyses were carried out separately for each outcome and type of study design (RCT/ cRCT). ... Meta-analysis was conducted only for interventions for which there were a minimum of two studies displaying sufficient homogeneity (I 2 statistic < 75%). ... The outcome abstraction from the trials was not limited to the primary outcome on which the trial was based. Efforts were made to pool results for all other reported outcomes ... Studies were pooled only if the outcomes had been measured in the same way by all studies.",
      "reason": "The review specifies how studies were grouped for syntheses (by outcome and study design RCT/cRCT), pooling rules (same measurement, minimum two studies, I2 threshold), linking groupings to the comparisons and objectives."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e5",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_13",
      "quote": "Only randomised controlled trials (community based randomised controlled trial, cluster randomised trials) published in the last 15 years (2000-2015) were included in the review. The time period was limited to base evidence on recently conducted studies in light of recent shift in delivery of primary health care services towards NCDs in most of the developing countries. It is worthwhile to highlight that till 2000, focus of the primary care services of most of the governments has been on maternal and child health services, family planning services, tuberculosis and HIV/AIDS.",
      "reason": "The review provides a rationale for the notable restriction on publication years (2000-2015), explaining the choice based on shifts in health service focus and relevance of recent evidence."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 90
}

{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_6",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_6_e1",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_13",
      "quote": "Searches of published literature on effectiveness of NCD control interventions delivered through community health worker under the programme (focus on developing countries) were done in the following biomedical, and general reference electronic databases, without restriction to language: PubMed (2000-2015); Excerpta Medica Database (EMBASE) (2000-2015); OVID (2000-2015) and World PLOS Health Organization (WHO) library and Cochrane library.",
      "reason": "The manuscript reports the coverage years (2000-2015) for several databases, but does not state the exact date on which each information source was last searched or consulted (e.g. day/month/year or single last-search date)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_6_e2",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_13",
      "quote": "PubMed (2000-2015); Excerpta Medica Database (EMBASE) (2000-2015); OVID (2000-2015) and World PLOS Health Organization (WHO) library and Cochrane library.",
      "reason": "The names of bibliographic databases and coverage years are reported; OVID is listed (a platform). However, the search interface/platform is not clearly specified for each database (e.g. PubMed interface details) and some items (WHO library/Cochrane) lack explicit platform/interface details."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_6_e3",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_13",
      "quote": \"Clinical trials registers such as ClinicalTrials.gov and portals to trials registers of different developing countries through (World Health Organization (WHO) International Clinical Trials Registry Platform, ICTRP) [20] were another source of information that were reviewed for relevant literature.\",
      "reason": "The manuscript names the study registers searched (ClinicalTrials.gov and WHO ICTRP) and the search timeframe for the review (2000-2015) is reported elsewhere, indicating the date restriction applied to these sources."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_6_e4",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_13",
      "quote": \"Website of the Health-Evidence.org was referred to for related reviews.\",
      "reason": "The manuscript names a website searched (Health-Evidence.org) but does not provide the URL for the site; other websites/search engines and their URLs are not reported."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_6_e5",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": "text_13",
      "quote": \"Authors or trial investigators for further information were contacted for queries pertaining to methodology, study outcome, availability of trial reports (if results not yet published as journal article).\",\      "reason": "The text indicates contacting authors or trial investigators but does not name any organisations or manufacturers that were contacted to identify studies."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_6_e6",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_13",
      "quote": \"Authors or trial investigators for further information were contacted for queries pertaining to methodology, study outcome, availability of trial reports (if results not yet published as journal article).\",\      "reason": "The manuscript specifies the types of individuals contacted (authors or trial investigators) to obtain further information about studies."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_6_e7",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_13",
      "quote": \"In addition, reference lists and bibliographies of previous systematic and non- systematic reviews were screened and citation tracking were undertaken to identify relevant studies.\",
      "reason": "The manuscript specifies the types of reference lists examined (reference lists and bibliographies of previous systematic and non-systematic reviews) and that citation tracking was used."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_6_e8",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_13",
      "quote": \"In addition, reference lists and bibliographies of previous systematic and non- systematic reviews were screened and citation tracking were undertaken to identify relevant studies.\",
      "reason": "The manuscript reports that citation tracking (backward/forward searching) was undertaken but does not report seed reports used for citation searching, the citation index/platform used, or the date the citation searches were run."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_6_e9",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": "text_5",
      "quote": \"Digital databases like PubMed, EMBASE, OVID, Cochrane library, dissertation abstracts, clinical trials registry web sites of different LMIC were searched for such publications between years 2000 and 2015.\",
      "reason": "The manuscript does not report consulting specific journals or conference proceedings by name, their covered dates, or the methods used to search them."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 65
}

